      ":question/worked-solution": "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=- \\frac{5}{2}$ and $Q(x)=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
